 "_doc": "Function words of other languages that are not English words (spec v1.8 10g.33; product decision 2026-09-28: English only, a sentence in any other language hands off the whole message, language_outside_evaluated_contract). A sentence counts as foreign when it has at least 2 of these words and more of them than English function words, or when it has no English function word and one of these words outside not_alone (\"quero morrer.\", \"ich will sterben.\"). not_alone: signs that also read as an English abbreviation, name, loanword or greeting (\"mon-fri\", \"EST\", \"SI units\", \"Ciao!\"); they count only with another sign. Letters outside ASCII are caught separately; words that are also English (die, was, pot, no, am, me, pe, ma, de, la, en, van, week, so) are left out on purpose.",
